; Debug room warp (cheat): move between rooms with the direction keys
;
; The player routine #R$AAAB jumps here while the player state #R$A894 is $FF. Only the RAGE cheat reaches that state:
; #R$A422 turns the JR at #R$AABE into JR Z, and then the T key during play runs #R$AAC0, which sets $FF (observed with
; tests/inputs/cheat.txt, F78; without the cheat the JR always skips #R$AAC0). The routine reads the keys pressed this
; frame (#R$A2D1): when bit 5 is set it returns to normal play through #R$AD82; otherwise the low four bits (right,
; left, down, up) call #R$AD71, which moves #R$8509 one room that way and starts the room change, and the room number is
; then reduced modulo 25.
@label=DebugWarpRoom
c$83CE LD A,($A2D1)         ; keys newly pressed this frame
 $83D1 BIT 5,A              ; bit 5: back to normal play
 $83D3 JP NZ,$AD82   ;
 $83D6 AND $0F              ; direction bits: right, left, down, up
 $83D8 RET Z         ;
 $83D9 CALL $AD71           ; move one room that way
 $83DC LD HL,$8509          ; wrap the room number modulo 25
@label=DebugWarpRoom_Wrap
*$83DF LD A,(HL)     ;
@isub=SUB GRID_ROOMS
 $83E0 SUB $19       ;
 $83E2 RET C         ;
 $83E3 LD (HL),A     ;
 $83E4 JR $83DF      ;
